{"name":"Augustus Asparagus","hex":"#90aa0b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"asparagus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various perennial plants of the genus Asparagus having leaflike stems, scalelike leaves, and small flowers.","The young shoots of Asparagus officinalis eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asparagus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Augustus","blocks":[{"text":"Augustus, also known as Octavian, was the founder of the Roman Empire and the first Roman emperor from 27 BC until his death in AD 14. The reign of Augustus initiated an imperial cult and an era of imperial peace when the Roman world was largely free of armed conflict. The principate, a style of government in which the emperor showed nominal deference to the Senate, was established during his reign and lasted until the Crisis of the Third Century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Augustus_of_Prima_Porta.jpg/330px-Augustus_of_Prima_Porta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus","wikidata":"Q1405"},{"title":"Asparagus","blocks":[{"text":"Asparagus or garden asparagus is a perennial flowering plant species in the genus Asparagus native to Eurasia. Widely cultivated as a vegetable crop, its young shoots are used as a spring vegetable. In 2024, world production of asparagus was 8.9 million tonnes, led by China with 87% of the total."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asparagus","wikidata":"Q28367"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png/330px-Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png/330px-Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreat_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/GaiusOctavius.jpg/500px-GaiusOctavius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/GaiusOctavius.jpg/500px-GaiusOctavius.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An idealized Roman sculpted portrait of Octavius as a teenager, possibly produced posthumously or when he was much older, now located in the Vatican Museums[23]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGaiusOctavius.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/RSC_0022_-_transparent_background.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/RSC_0022_-_transparent_background.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Denarius from 44 BC, showing Julius Caesar on the obverse and the goddess Venus on the reverse of the coin. Caption: CAESAR IMP. M. / L. AEMILIVS BVCA","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARSC_0022_-_transparent_background.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Vincenzo_Camuccini_-_La_morte_di_Cesare.jpg/500px-Vincenzo_Camuccini_-_La_morte_di_Cesar